 ## [Unreleased]
 
+### Added
+
+- `ToolRegistry` now compiles each registered tool's `inputSchema` with `ajv` and validates
+  model-supplied tool input in `ToolRegistry.execute` before invoking the executor. Invalid
+  schemas on static tool definitions throw at `register` time naming the tool; runtime input
+  rejections return a `ToolResponse` naming the failing field paths and constraints (without
+  echoing or logging property values) so the model can correct the call on the next tool round.
+
+### Changed
+
+- **Migration note for tool executors:** `ToolRegistry.execute` now enforces `required`,
+  declared property types, and `enum` from each tool's `inputSchema` before calling its
+  executor (while passing undeclared extra properties through unmodified without type coercion
+  or defaults). An executor that used to hand-validate its input now receives only input the
+  schema already accepts, and a tool that relied on seeing malformed input to produce its own
+  error message stops seeing it because `ToolRegistry.execute` returns the rejection
+  `ToolResponse` directly to the model.
+
